  ],
  "description": "JH-400B series input module 43E241, technical manual dated January 1, 1978, Figure 20. Channel mic input to the preamp-out patch point in mic mode. The two-pole balanced input pad and 10 kΩ gain rheostat are live. The phantom feed is open. Source impedance is 150 Ω balanced. R106 is the original 10 kΩ termination; the patch receiver is high impedance. T1 uses a representative Jensen 1:10 winding model, with JT-115K-E DC resistances and estimated inductances. Q102 and Q101 use 2N3904 and 2N3906 transport cards for the original S39568 and S39569. The MCI2001 card includes effective internal frequency compensation. Fader, equalizer and channel summing are downstream of this patch point.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Mic gain"
    ]
  },
  "name": "MCI JH-400B Mic Preamp 43E241",
